      "text": "From the original problem, we know that the slope of the given line is $m = -\\frac{2}{3}$. According to the property that the slope of a line perpendicular to another line is the negative reciprocal of the original line's slope, we have the slope of the desired line as \\[\n-\\frac{1}{-}\\frac{2}{3} = \\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the slope of the line that is perpendicular to $2x + 3y = 6$ is $\\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}$.",
